.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt LATENCY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm latency
.Nd watch scheduling and interrupt delays
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar priority
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl st Ar threshold
.Op Fl it Ar threshold
.Op Fl c Ar codefile
.Op Fl l Ar logfile
.Op Fl R Ar rawfile
.Op Fl n Ar kernel
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows delays in thread scheduling and interrupt handling, using the kernel
trace facility.
Unless given
.Fl R ,
it must run as root.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl p Ar priority
Watch this scheduling priority, or a range such as 31-47.
.It Fl h
Show interrupt delays at high resolution.
Write them to
.Pa latencies.csv
on exit.
.It Fl m
Report interrupt delays for each CPU.
.It Fl st Ar threshold
Log trace entries when a scheduling delay exceeds this many microseconds.
.It Fl it Ar threshold
Log trace entries when an interrupt delay exceeds this many microseconds.
.It Fl c Ar codefile
Read trace code names from this file.
The default is
.Pa /usr/share/misc/trace.codes .
.It Fl l Ar logfile
Write trace entries to this file when a threshold is exceeded.
.It Fl R Ar rawfile
Process this raw trace file.
.It Fl n Ar kernel
Read symbols from this kernel file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sc_usage 1
